    },
    {
      "type": "TALK",
      "content": "I’d say affordability is usually the hardest, because the other priorities all have to fit within it. More floor space can make privacy easier, while additional windows can improve daylight—but both affect the budget. Flexibility can get expensive too, if it relies on complicated movable walls.\n\nI’d rather standardise the structure and service areas, then design a room that can work as either a bedroom or a study, with a proper door and daylight. That gives people options without making the default needlessly costly. Your search comparison is spot on: the default should work well before anyone has to customise it.",
      "target": "Lisa Carter",
      "images": null
    },
    {
      "type": "DONE",
