    "description": "Philip spent most of his career on road, bridge, and municipal utility projects. He moved from field engineering into estimating and operations management, coordinating subcontractors, schedules, equipment, budgets, and communication with public-agency clients. He retired from full-time work at 70. He now accepts occasional, narrowly defined assignments reviewing schedules and contract documentation for former contacts, averaging roughly 12 to 18 billable hours a month when work is available. He no longer maintains an active engineering license and does not sign engineering documents.",
    "work_attitude": "He enjoys solving a concrete problem and being paid for his judgment, but turns down work that would keep him on call during a vacation. He sometimes finds it hard to stop revising a report after the client has what it needs."
