  "financial_situation": {
    "household_income": "Approximately $245,000 before taxes in 2025, including about $52,000 in combined pension income, $63,000 in Social Security benefits, $77,000 in dividends, interest, and realized investment gains, $35,000 from Philip's consulting, and $18,000 in net rental income. Investment and consulting income vary from year to year.",
    "assets_and_obligations": "Philip and Helen own their home and one rental property. They have substantial retirement savings, but he thinks of their investment income as less dependable than their pensions. Property upkeep, insurance premiums, taxes, and possible future long-term care costs make him reluctant to treat their income as entirely available for spending.",
